<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Acts of the Scillitan Martyrs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">180</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Acts of the Scillitan Martyrs is a short <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> record of the trial at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> on 17 July 180 of twelve Christians from the town of Scilli in Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. Refusing to swear by the emperor's genius, they were condemned and beheaded on the order of the proconsul Vigellius Saturninus. It is the earliest dated Christian document in Latin and the first evidence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p></div>
